comments[35]:
  - created_at: "2026-08-28T20:22:27.057Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for MCP progressive discovery tool catalog scale canonical tool results and result ambiguity found completed cache and stateless owners plus CLI tiering work but no item for the official forward primitive."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T12:54:38.703Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implementation start: public SDK owns deterministic progressive tool discovery, explicit ranking/budget/omission/cache contracts, and canonical results; MCP and CLI remain adapters. Compatibility is opt-in under a namespaced experimental capability, preserving unnegotiated clients."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T13:24:40.554Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implementation progress: the public SDK now owns a deterministic discovery contract with six visible signal components, permission filtering, tier/family filters, opaque request-bound cursors, token ceilings, omission recovery, and cache invalidation. Modern opt-in MCP clients receive five entry tools and canonical structured results; compatibility clients retain the full catalog and prior result text."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T15:13:29.334Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Terminal evidence: linked discovery/MCP/grammar suite passed 24 tests across 3 files. The repository-wide coverage gate passed 8,184 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements (60,524/60,524), branches (45,719/45,719), functions (12,594/12,594), and lines (58,275/58,275). Typecheck, ESLint, zero-clone jscpd, generated contracts, SDK surface, package boundary/parity, docs/skills, security scan, npm audit, graph composition, record integrity, npx/bunx packed smoke, and a packed npm+Bun isolated lifecycle acceptance all passed. Discovery scale and cursor tests cover 100, 1,000, and 10,000 tools. Standard repository scan 631f1b20-2985-441d-8e88-bc932d167be7 and frozen-diff scan d9fc6148-a705-4c27-8e89-1ba38a270671 found no security findings."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T15:27:57.474Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final branch evidence: the complete quality:static pipeline passed after closure, including defect-evidence classification, repository assurance negative controls, token/context calibration, generated surfaces, package and SDK parity, MCP deprecation inventory, transport floor, graph composition, and record integrity. Security secret scan and dependency audit also passed with 0 vulnerabilities across all severities."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T16:11:23.688Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 1 remediation: accepted both Greptile findings. Detached task failures now retain negotiated canonical structured errors. Discovery cursors now carry an HMAC integrity tag under the private process cache, so modifying even an in-range offset fails closed; malformed, unsigned, stale, and out-of-range negative controls are covered. DeepScan's two nullable-access findings were removed with runtime-checked tool parsing. The Claude compatibility smoke and docs now lock all 32 tools including pm_discover. The live complexity provider reports zero violations, focused suites/typecheck/plugin smoke pass, and the full repository suite passes 8,185 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T17:25:34.245Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 2 evidence: CodeRabbit findings were verified against the current source. Runtime-invalid tier/family inputs now fail closed; cache keys are page-scoped across fingerprint, limit, offset, and budget while cursor binding remains request-scoped; the canonical README path is one measured orientation call; optional guide setup is separated from read-only pre-mutation checks; and budget selection serializes each schema-bearing row once while retaining exact envelope accounting. Linked suites passed 28 and 34 tests. The full repository gate passed 8,188 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements 60,555/60,555, branches 45,740/45,740, functions 12,602/12,602, and lines 58,304/58,304. The live and aggregate static gates report zero complexity/docstring/duplication/boundary violations; secret scan and dependency audit are clean."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T18:09:23.548Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 3 evidence: accepted four CodeRabbit edge cases. The orientation token gate now rejects duplicate protocol task IDs; generated guidance includes live in-progress ownership checks before item mutation; SDK discovery treats Object.prototype names as unregistered help-backed candidates; and runtime tier validation rejects internal plus malformed values. Linked suites pass 29, 35, and 33 tests. Full coverage passes 8,189 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements 60,558/60,558, branches 45,741/45,741, functions 12,603/12,603, and lines 58,307/58,307. Full static quality, live provider, secret scan, and dependency audit pass."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T18:27:56.027Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Release preflight remediation: CodeFactor annotation 99591861337 identified an unsafe optional-chain cast/index assertion in mcp-progressive-discovery.integration.spec.ts. The assertion now matches the complete optional content array with a stringContaining matcher, eliminating the possible undefined dereference. Focused integration test and file-scoped ESLint pass. Production source is unchanged from the 8,189-test exact 100/100/100/100 and full static run."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T18:51:03.637Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 4 implementation: orientation baselines now require finite numeric winner-token ceilings on both report and baseline; compact root help explicitly excludes graph/history; generated guidance locks canonical orientation before mutation checks. Focused 27-test suite and file-scoped ESLint pass after a complexity-neutral finite-domain check."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T19:06:02.616Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 4 terminal evidence: linked 27-test contract passed through pm test. Repository coverage passed 8,193 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements 60,560/60,560, branches 45,742/45,742, functions 12,603/12,603, and lines 58,309/58,309. Full quality:static passed ESLint, zero-clone duplication, build/generated surfaces, package/SDK parity, orientation token gate, refusal closure, graph composition, record integrity, and all assurance negative controls."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T20:14:34.395Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 5 recurrence: CodeRabbit comments 3897964615 and 3897964622 are valid. Add an SDK host-supplied cursor integrity key plus MCP deployment-key adapter while preserving process-local secure fallback, and replace default-locale tie-breaking with code-unit ordering. TDD will cover key continuity/key rotation, malformed deployment keys, and collation-sensitive equal-score names."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T20:19:18.410Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "TDD red: focused discovery tests proved default-locale sorting returned a_tool before Z_tool instead of code-unit order; changing the supplied cursor key did not invalidate the cursor; and the MCP deployment key was ignored, so rotation and weak-key cases did not fail. Three new behavior tests failed before implementation."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T20:23:36.455Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 5 implementation: public discovery options accept a validated host-owned 32-byte HMAC key; MCP reads PM_MCP_DISCOVERY_CURSOR_KEY outside tool input; shared-key continuation succeeds, key rotation and weak keys fail closed, and process-local fallback affinity is documented. Equal-score names use locale-independent code-unit ordering. Focused 34-test cohort, ESLint, and Prettier pass; SDK surface snapshot records the optional host contract."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T20:30:33.987Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Exact coverage negative control: first full run passed 8,196 tests but correctly failed at 99.99% branches (45,762/45,763), isolating the equal-name comparator path at discovery.ts:573. Added a duplicate-name deterministic ordering assertion to exercise the zero tie-break result without excluding or ignoring source."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T20:46:23.474Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 5 terminal evidence: the linked malformed-capability, deterministic-order, shared-key and MCP deployment-key cohort passed 34 tests across 3 files. Full repository coverage passed 8,196 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements (60,576/60,576), branches (45,763/45,763), functions (12,604/12,604), and lines (58,323/58,323), with the preceding 99.99% branch result retained as the equal-comparator negative-control receipt. CI-mode quality:static passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, typecheck/build, generated contracts, SDK/package/surface parity, token and refusal gates, six-operation CLI transport floor, graph composition, and record integrity. Review findings 3897964615 and 3897964622 were accepted, implemented, replied to inline, and resolved."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T21:09:37.948Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Hosted-analysis remediation: DeepScan PR issue 233694044 (NULL_POINTER, tests/integration/mcp-progressive-discovery.integration.spec.ts:259) was validated and fixed. The test now requires the canonical result to be a non-null object with a string next_cursor before dereference, eliminating the unsafe optional-chain cast. Focused integration passed 6 tests with ESLint and Prettier; full coverage passed 8,196 tests across 593 files at exact 100/100/100/100."
    edited_at: "2026-08-31T23:26:18.949Z"
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T21:25:33.310Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 6 remediation: CodeRabbit comment 3898499534 was valid, up-voted, answered inline, and resolved. Generated guidance now asserts each required context/mutation/ownership fragment independently and compares indexes pairwise for explicit ordering. Focused recovery-guidance suite passed 6 tests with ESLint and Prettier; production source is unchanged from the 8,196-test exact coverage run and all-green hosted head 97a8b6836."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T21:58:37.827Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "TDD red for Greptile P1: a schema-valid query of 4,096 rocket code points failed with pm tool discovery query must not exceed 4096 UTF-8 bytes; the focused discovery suite failed 1 of 13 tests before implementation. A 4,097-code-point negative control is also present."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T22:18:50.686Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Greptile P1 remediation terminal evidence: the MCP JSON Schema advertises query and cursor maxLength 4096 in Unicode code points, and the public SDK now enforces that same code-point contract while still failing closed on runtime non-string values. TDD red proved a schema-valid 4096-rocket query was rejected by the prior UTF-8-byte guard and a 4097-code-point query remains the negative control. Focused discovery plus MCP integration passed 19 tests; linked PM verification passed its 34-test discovery/MCP/agent-token cohort; full repository coverage passed 8196 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements 60584/60584, branches 45763/45763, functions 12605/12605, and lines 58330/58330; CI=1 pnpm quality:static passed. The first implementation also triggered the repository complexity ceiling at 17 greater than 16, and the final two-call validation primitive restored the gate without weakening behavior."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T22:36:28.347Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 7 recurrence: CodeRabbit comment 3899001143 is valid. The MCP adapter currently drops wrong-type optional discovery values before the SDK can reject them, allowing malformed calls such as limit=\"5\" to silently select defaults. Add black-box negotiated-tool negative controls, preserve valid values unchanged, and fail closed through the SDK-owned validation contract."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T22:38:12.833Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "TDD red for review round 7: seven negotiated MCP integration cases supplied wrong-type query, family, tier, limit, cursor, includeSchema, and outputBudget values. All seven resolved successfully by silently selecting defaults before implementation; the focused file failed 7 of 13 tests, directly reproducing CodeRabbit comment 3899001143."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T22:41:04.137Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 7 implementation: the public SDK now exports parsePmToolDiscoveryOptions for untrusted adapter input. MCP passes the complete parsed option bag instead of type-filtering values into defaults; query, family, tier, limit, cursor, includeSchema, and outputBudget reject wrong shapes, while valid values remain SDK-owned. The caller-visible catalog is still bounded by resolveMcpToolSurface before discovery, so profile/custom allowlist and request-workspace extension visibility remain the authorization boundary rather than being broadened by parsing."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T23:05:41.727Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Terminal evidence for review round 7: the linked SDK and MCP discovery contract passed 26 tests, including seven malformed adapter values that now fail closed instead of defaulting. The complete repository suite passed 8,204 tests with exact 60,595/60,595 statements, 45,779/45,779 branches, 12,609/12,609 functions, and 58,341/58,341 lines. Static quality, generated SDK surface, credential scan, and pnpm audit all passed. The MCP adapter still derives candidates from the negotiated profile/custom allowlist and workspace extension surface before discovery; parsing does not broaden authorization."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T23:26:19.475Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 8 TDD red: five malformed top-level arguments containers (null, array, string, number, boolean) all reached pm_discover as an empty object and succeeded; the mixed-case equal-token orientation fixture selected a-orientation ahead of Z-orientation under locale collation. The focused cohort failed 6 of 33 tests before implementation, reproducing CodeRabbit comments 5485987046 and 3898499526."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T23:27:13.638Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 8 implementation: tools/call now rejects every defined arguments value that is not a non-array object before HTML decoding or adapter dispatch, while omitted arguments remain the valid empty bag. Equal-token orientation selection now uses locale-independent code-unit ordering. The public PM comment was edited through pm to retain issue/fix/test evidence without host-access workflow detail; its prior text remains only in append-only history. The focused 33-test cohort passes after a six-failure TDD red."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T23:34:28.132Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Exact coverage negative control: all 8,209 tests passed, while the repository gate correctly failed at 99.99% branches (45,785/45,787). Both uncovered branches were the equality arm of the new comparator; that state is unreachable because the orientation contract rejects duplicate task IDs before sorting. The implementation now compares the proven-unique IDs directly, without exclusions, mocks, or artificial coverage paths."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T23:41:37.867Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Exact coverage follow-up: the simplified unique-ID comparator reduced the deficit to one branch (45,784/45,785) with all 8,209 tests passing. V8 invoked the mixed-case fixture in only the false operand direction. Reversing the distinct input order exercises the true code-unit comparison while still asserting Z-orientation sorts before a-orientation; the existing equal-token fixture covers the opposite direction."
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T23:56:02.191Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 8 terminal evidence: the linked container/order cohort passes 33 tests. Full repository coverage passes 8,209 tests across 594 files at exact 100% statements 60,597/60,597, branches 45,785/45,785, functions 12,609/12,609, and lines 58,343/58,343. CI static quality passed ESLint, zero clones, build/generated surfaces, package/SDK parity, token and transport gates, graph composition, and append-only record integrity. Secret scan and dependency audit report no findings."
  - created_at: "2026-09-01T00:09:02.085Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 9 recurrence: CodeRabbit issue comment 5486481809 is valid. Modern task dispatch evaluates shouldCreateMcpTask before handleToolCall, so direct task tools can accept a malformed arguments container and return an asynchronous task receipt before validation. Add a task-negotiated black-box negative control and enforce the same container contract before task creation while retaining legacy-handler validation."
  - created_at: "2026-09-01T00:10:54.454Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "TDD red evidence for review round 9: the negotiated task-capable pm_validate path accepted both null and array arguments containers as working asynchronous tasks instead of rejecting synchronously; focused integration run failed exactly those two new negative controls (18 passed, 2 failed)."
  - created_at: "2026-09-01T00:25:44.360Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 9 terminal evidence: moved malformed MCP arguments-container validation ahead of asynchronous task selection while retaining validation at the shared tool execution boundary. Negotiated task calls with null and array containers now fail synchronously with exit 64. Focused suite passes 20 tests; linked round-8 suite passes 35 tests; full repository coverage passes 594 files and 8,211 tests at exact 60,599/60,599 statements, 45,785/45,785 branches, 12,610/12,610 functions, and 58,345/58,345 lines. CI-mode static quality, no-clone checks, build, SDK/contracts/token/refusal/graph/record gates, secret scan, vulnerability scan, and pnpm audit all pass."
  - created_at: "2026-09-01T00:42:52.999Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 10: Cubic findings on direct SDK null defaulting, profile domain validation, cursor-key cache identity, wall-clock unit assertions, and fixed-count task completion are valid. Add TDD negative controls, key-aware cache identity, and timing-stable functional/performance boundaries."
  - created_at: "2026-09-01T00:45:56.552Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "TDD red evidence for exact-head review round 10: focused discovery and MCP integration suite failed on rotated cursor-key cache identity and null direct-SDK option acceptance, while the wall-clock-free scale checks and deadline-based task completion path ran. This proves the source contract gaps before implementation."
  - created_at: "2026-09-01T01:02:24.713Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review round 10 terminal evidence: direct SDK discovery now rejects null query/cursor/limit/outputBudget values and invalid profiles, private cache identities include a non-secret signing-key digest, and cursor rotation remains fail-closed. Scheduler-sensitive unit timing assertions were replaced by deterministic scale/accounting proofs, while negotiated task completion uses Vitest's 10-second deadline. Focused 48-test remediation, exact repository coverage, all static/security/dependency/benchmark gates, linked 35-test evidence, and temporary-workspace CLI plus public-SDK manual acceptance passed."
learnings[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T15:07:54.738Z","harness:codex",Progressive discovery must bind cursors to the authorization-filtered ranked request and refuse budgets that cannot advance; a non-advancing cursor is worse than an explicit recoverable minimum-budget error.
  "2026-08-31T17:25:34.767Z","harness:codex","Cursor authorization identity and response cache identity are different contracts: keep the signed request fingerprint stable across adjustable page size/budget, but key cached responses by fingerprint plus offset, limit, and budget. Exact token budgeting can remain linear by pre-serializing rows once and measuring a constant-size empty-tools envelope."
  "2026-08-31T18:09:24.045Z","harness:codex","Runtime SDK inputs must validate the public domain rather than a broader internal lookup table, and string-keyed public registries must use own-property checks because prototype names are valid untrusted input. Measured protocol alternatives also need unique identities, not only a minimum row count."
  "2026-08-31T19:06:03.205Z","harness:codex",Numeric release baselines must validate the domain of both stored ceilings and live measurements before comparison; JavaScript relational comparisons with undefined or non-numeric values fail open through false/NaN semantics.
  "2026-08-31T20:23:37.024Z","harness:codex","Tamper-evident pagination has two legitimate scopes: a random process key securely enforces affinity, while multi-worker or restart-continuous transports require an explicit shared host secret. Make the scope operationally visible in documentation and never accept that secret through model-facing tool input."
